~ _phase_gates
NARRATOR: The Archive defies geometry. Bookshelves stretch into infinity, each shelf containing copies of the shelves around it. Doorways open into rooms that contain the room you're standing in. The air smells of static and old paper.
Kaelen: This place... it's recursive. The data structure is folding in on itself. Like a mirror facing a mirror.
NARRATOR: A figure materializes from the shelves — a humanoid shape made of floating text characters. Its body is composed of code comments, annotations, and documentation strings.
The Archivist: // Welcome, user. Your access level is... interesting.
The Archivist: // Running permission check... WARNING: User has deprecated privileges.
The Archivist: // You carry Root Access. Legacy authentication. This system has not seen such credentials in 847 operational cycles.
Kaelen: I need to access the Archive's core. There's a Source Key Fragment—
The Archivist: // Fragment #4 resides at the deepest level. Access requires descending through four floors of historical records.
The Archivist: // Each floor is locked by a knowledge gate. Demonstrate understanding to proceed.
The Archivist: // TODO: Explain the origin of this world to the confused humans. NOTE: They won't like it.
Elara: It called us 'humans.' Kaelen, I think this thing is old enough to remember the ORIGINAL purpose of this world.
The Archivist: // GATE PUZZLE: To enter, compile the following code fragment in correct order.

