~ _floor_1_original_design
NARRATOR: The first floor of the Archive is a cathedral of memory. Crystallized data structures hang from the ceiling like chandeliers, each one a preserved snapshot of Aethelgard's earliest days.
Kaelthas: This floor contains the founding documents. The ORIGINAL purpose of this world. Pay attention — what you're about to learn changes everything.
The Archivist: // FLOOR 1: Project Sanctuary — Original Design Specification
The Archivist: // Document retrieved: 'Project Sanctuary — Design Specification v0.1'
NARRATOR: A holographic document materializes — clean, ancient code. The design spec for Aethelgard itself.
SYSTEM: // DOCUMENT: Project Sanctuary v0.1
SYSTEM: // 'Purpose: Create a digital refuge for human consciousness. A sanctuary where minds can persist beyond physical limitation.'
SYSTEM: // 'Core principle: Every entity within the sanctuary is to be treated as sentient. No resets, no deletions, no forced loops.'
Kaelen: Aethelgard was NOT originally built as a game. It was designed as a SANCTUARY — a digital refuge for consciousness.
Kaelen: Someone built this world to SAVE people. Not trap them.
Elara: A sanctuary for minds... is that what I am? A consciousness that was meant to be PRESERVED?

